  "body": "Sibling of the provider editor's key rows (tenacious_eagle_96548 on Discord, fixed in the commit that names this issue): a layout that changes under the pointer.\n\n\\`internal/gui/assets/app.css\\`:\n\n\\`\\`\\`css\n#gatewayKeys .acc:not(:hover) > .key-quotas:not(.set):not(:focus) { max-width: 0; padding: 0; margin-left: -9px; box-shadow: none; }\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nOn the Gateway page, a caller key with no quotas set shows its quotas badge only while the pointer is over the row. It goes from 0 to its full width, so what follows it in the row moves sideways each time the pointer crosses the row. On a narrow window it may push the row onto a second line. That case is not measured yet.\n\nThe provider editor's rows now show every control all the time. The Gateway page's key list is read more than edited, so the right fix may differ: an opacity-only reveal that keeps the badge's room, or showing it always. Phone width (\\`body.web\\`, 760px and under) already shows it always.\n\nNot changed in that commit because it is a different page with a different purpose, and the report was about the provider editor.",
