   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5676-gateway-key-badges-no-shift), commit [824152e8b](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/824152e8b57d1a02c1ad00ef04b348dae562d506), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe rule that collapsed a key's unset quota and concurrency badges to zero width is gone, so the row no longer moves when the pointer crosses it: on the built app the measured coordinates are identical before and after hover (the base moved \"All models\" by about 165px). Below magpie's 760px phone width the row wraps and the unset badges stay readable instead of being squeezed to a sliver; 521-600px desktop had left the concurrency badge unreadable, which is why the breakpoint matches the `body.web` layout.\n\nEvidence comes from the real built app in a real browser with fake keys: before/after hover coordinates at desktop and 420/521/600/760px, a long key name plus an MCP badge without page overflow, a visible focus ring, and an Enter toggle checked event-driven (no waits, no sleeps). The bundled Playwright suite was not run (unavailable here); a native desktop host was not exercised; the full `nogui` build passes. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
